<section class="page-hero"><div class="container page-hero__content"><p class="eyebrow">Cookie policy</p><h1>Essential technology, used thoughtfully.</h1><p class="lead">This policy explains the limited use of cookies and similar technologies on this website.</p></div></section>

<section class="section section--pearl"><article class="container legal-copy">
    <p class="legal-updated">Last updated: 25 September 2026</p>
    <p>Cookies are small text files stored by your browser. Private Jet Executive uses essential cookies and similar session technology to make the website secure and functional.</p>
    <h2>Essential cookies</h2><p>When you use the contact or charter enquiry forms, we use the <strong>pje_session</strong> session cookie. It helps protect the forms from unauthorised submissions, preserve your secure session while you complete a request, and apply sensible rate limits. It is a session cookie and normally expires when you close your browser.</p>
    <h2>What we do not currently use</h2><p>We do not currently set advertising, marketing or analytics cookies through this website. If that changes, this policy will be updated before those technologies are used.</p>
    <h2>Managing cookies</h2><p>You can control or delete cookies through your browser settings. Blocking essential cookies may prevent the enquiry forms from working correctly. Browser settings differ, so please refer to your browser’s help information for instructions.</p>
    <h2>Contact and updates</h2><p>If you have a question about this policy, contact <a href="mailto:charter@privatejetexecutive.com">charter@privatejetexecutive.com</a>. We may update this policy when the website or our use of cookies changes.</p>
</article></section>
